            <ArticleTitle>[Symptom-oriented assessment in AIDS patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>504-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The differential diagnosis of recently acquired cough, diarrhea, headaches, odynophagia and fever in AIDS-Patients is discussed. The aim is to find the most frequent, the treatable and the most dangerous diseases. We discuss the empirical and the symptomatic treatment in special situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
